Z||000007||Fformula88||11-02-2001||10:27 PM||||The names surrounding my Fiero really aren't appropriate for a public forum!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I usually use them around repair work... especially the torturous job of replacing the 88 brakes!<P>An old gf once told me I should name my cars because they have feelings and won't break done as much if they feel loved.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  Wierdest thing was when we were about to go on a trip, she got in the car (my Ford Probe), petted the dash board and told the car it was a good car, asking it to be good and not break down!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  It ran perfectly for the weekend trip... put on 1500 miles... but two months later the transmission died.  Maybe the car missed the affection?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>As a side note... for a weekend she completely filled the cavernous hatchback trunk of my car, which is why I declined to take the Fiero!||||reg||1
