Z||000020||Brian87egotrip||11-03-2001||09:24 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fformula88:<BR><B><BR>An old gf once told me I should name my cars because they have feelings and won't break done as much if they feel loved.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">   Wierdest thing was when we were about to go on a trip, she got in the car (my Ford Probe), petted the dash board and told the car it was a good car, asking it to be good and not break down!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  It ran perfectly for the weekend trip... put on 1500 miles... but two months later the transmission died.  Maybe the car missed the affection?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I believe that too. On run for the hills one year when I was coming home I petted the dash and told her what a good job she did in the mountains, now if she could just make it home. She did and then died the next morning. But she did what I asked her too. <P>------------------<BR>Brian                    87GT||||reg||1
